// A landing party on a tile map, with no Python.
//
// Everything the crew meets on the ground is written in this file. The ground itself is
// `ground/landing.tiles` (the map) and `ground/starter.tileset` (what can be walked).
// story.mast holds only the logic that reacts: it reads this file, loads the ground with
// one line, and opens the landing party when the ship reaches the relay.
//
// A record is `### [Display Name](key)`, an optional `---` fenced block of fields, then
// body prose. Comments are `//` - note that .mast uses `#` instead.

# [Kesh Relay](kesh_relay)


// ---- The crew: who sits at each console, and so who goes down. You beam down as the
// person you have been all evening. `Roles:` is what a choice asks for (`if medical`).
// `Skills:` is what a `check` rolls with: a ten sided die, plus the skill, plus one for
// each crew member standing beside you who has it.
## [The Watch](crew)
---
crew
Ship: Artemis
---
The watch aboard when Kesh Relay went dark.

### [Lt Dana Ross](ross)
---
Console: helm
Roles: helm
Skills: helm 4, engineering 1
---

### [Lt Sam Reyes](reyes)
---
Console: weapons
Roles: security
Skills: security 4, athletics 2
---

### [Dr Ines Hale](hale)
---
Console: science
Roles: medical, science
Skills: medical 4, science 3
---

### [Chief Okoro](okoro)
---
Console: engineering
Roles: engineering
Skills: engineering 4, science 1
---

### [Ens Tam Vale](vale)
---
Console: comms
Roles: comms
Skills: comms 3, science 2
---


// ---- Quests. `Scope: shared` is one copy for the whole crew.
//
// HOW THE GAME ENDS. `Win:` and `Lose:` are the last sentence the crew reads. COMPLETING
// a quest that has `Win:` wins the game with it; FAILING a quest that has `Lose:` loses
// it. A choice in a scene does either one: `; completes relight` or `; fails relight`
// (see The Beacon, at the end of this file).
## [Quests](quests)

### [Relight Kesh Relay](relight)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: at once
Objective: Light the beacon at Kesh Relay
Leads to: beacon
Win: The beacon is lit. Every convoy on the Kesh run has its way home again.
Lose: The beacon is slag. The Kesh run stays dark, and the convoys must find another road.
---
The relay's beacon went dark nine days ago. Go down and light it.

// `reach relay 6000` waits for a ship within 6000 of anything with the ROLE `relay` -
// story.mast gives the station that role. `Then: signal relay_reached` is what opens the
// landing party: story.mast has one route waiting on exactly that name.
### [Hold at the Relay](arrive)
---
Scope: shared
Starts when: at once
Objective: Close to within 6000 of Kesh Relay
Done when: reach relay 6000
Then: signal relay_reached
---
Bring the ship in close enough for a transporter lock.


// ---- Side stories: a quest for ONE person. `For:` is a job from a `Roles:` line (or a
// crew member's key). Each is handed to its person when they beam down; one nobody on
// the ground answers to is handed to nobody. `Leads to:` names what it points at, by key.
## [Side Stories](side_stories)

### [The Caretaker's Cough](cough)
---
For: medical
Starts when: at once
Objective: See to the caretaker
Done when: signal marrow_treated
Leads to: marrow
---
The man who kept the relay has been breathing its dust for nine days.

// When somebody on the ground is put down for good, the game sends the signal
// `hostile_down_` and their key.
### [Clear the Yard](clear_yard)
---
For: security
Starts when: at once
Objective: Put the relay's sentry out of action
Done when: signal hostile_down_sentry
Leads to: sentry
---
The sentry does not know a friend from a thief any more.


// ---- Props: things on the ground. `Area:` is the area file it stands in, and `Mark:` a
// mark in that file (or `At: x, y`, a cell). What a prop DOES is whichever of these it
// has: `Scene:` opens a scene for whoever uses it, `Item:` is picked up into their pack,
// `Opens with:` makes it a door. `Blocks: yes` means nobody walks through it.
// `Scan:` is what the device's Scan app says about it.
## [Props](props)

### [Yard terminal](terminal)
---
Area: landing
Mark: terminal
Sprite: prop:terminal
Scene: terminal
Blocks: yes
Scan: Still drawing a trickle of power. Its last entry is nine days old.
---
A weatherproof terminal beside the relay door, its screen still lit.

// A DOOR. `Opens with:` is tried in order by whoever uses it: a key anyone in the party
// is carrying, a skill check, a CUT shot from the device, or a signal - here the one the
// terminal sends once somebody has the door code.
### [Relay door](door)
---
Area: landing
Mark: door
Sprite: prop:hatch
Open sprite: prop:doorframe
Blocks: yes
Opens with: key relay_key, check engineering 9, cut, signal relay_unlocked
Scan: Mag locked. The keycard reader beside it is live.
---
The only way into the relay house. Shut, and meant to stay that way.

// A PICKUP. Using it puts `relay_key` in the pack of whoever picked it up.
### [Relay keycard](keycard)
---
Area: landing
Mark: keycard
Sprite: prop:keycard
Item: relay_key
---
A gray keycard on a lanyard, dropped where the sentry walks.

// HIDDEN until a signal. It is not on the map at all until `cache_known` is sent - which
// the caretaker's scene does, further down.
### [Medical kit](cache)
---
Area: landing
Mark: cache
Sprite: prop:crate_medical
Item: medkit
Hidden until: cache_known
---
A sealed medical kit under camouflage netting.

### [The beacon](beacon)
---
Area: landing
Mark: beacon
Sprite: prop:beacon
Scene: beacon
Blocks: yes
Scan: No power in the lamp. The socket for its cell is empty.
---
The relay's beacon: a lamp the height of two people, dark.

// SCENERY. A prop with no scene, no item, no lock and no words is furniture: it is drawn
// and it blocks, and nothing offers to use it.
### [Tent](tent)
---
Area: landing
Mark: tent
Sprite: prop:tent
Blocks: yes
---


// ---- People: someone you can walk up to and talk with. `Calm: yes` means they never
// attack. `Talk scene:` is the scene a click on them opens. `Face:` is shown beside what
// they say (`male`, `female`, or a face string).
## [People](people)

### [Old Marrow](marrow)
---
Area: landing
Mark: caretaker
Sprite: fig:junker_m
Face: male
Calm: yes
Talk scene: marrow
Scan: One human. Elevated pulse, and a wet cough.
---
The relay's caretaker, sitting on an upturned crate beside his tent.


// ---- Hostiles: someone who walks a `Patrol:` (cells, `x y; x y`), notices a crew member
// within `Notice:` cells, and attacks. `HP:` is how much it takes; `Stun:` how many
// seconds a stun shot holds it; `Drops:` what it leaves where it falls.
## [Hostiles](hostiles)

### [Relay sentry](sentry)
---
Area: landing
Mark: sentry
Sprite: fig:robot_war
HP: 2
Damage: 1
Notice: 4
Stun: 10
Speed: 2
Patrol: 20 9; 26 9; 26 11; 20 11
Drops: power_cell
Scan: Security frame, nine days without a recognition update. One power cell.
---
A security frame walking the same square it has walked for nine days.


// ---- Scenes: what is said, and what can be answered. Each `%` line is something the
// scene may say (one is picked). Each `-` line is a choice: `[words](where it leads)`,
// then `if <who may take it>`, then `; <what it does>`. An empty `()` ends the scene.
//
// WHO: a job (`if medical`), how good (`if skill science >= 3`), what they carry
// (`if holding power_cell`), or what the party has worked out - how many things
// (`if learned >= 2`) or one named thing (`if learned codes`).
//
// WHAT IT DOES: `learn <fact>`, `signal <name>`, `take <item>`, `give <item>`,
// `check <skill> <number> else <scene>` (a failed roll goes to that scene instead),
// `completes <quest>`, `fails <quest>`.
## [Scenes](scenes)

### [The Yard Terminal](terminal)
%{learned codes < 1} One line on the screen, over and over: DOOR SEALED. AWAITING CODE.
%{learned codes} DOOR SEALED. AWAITING CODE. And now you have one to give it.

- [Read the log](terminal_log) ; learn log
- [Pull the door code out of its memory](terminal_code) if skill science >= 3
- [Force the service port](terminal_code) ; check engineering 8 else terminal_dead
- [Send the door code](terminal_sent) if learned codes ; signal relay_unlocked
- [Step back]()

### [Nine Days](terminal_log)
% Day one: beacon cell failing. Day two: cell removed for test and fitted to the sentry, which has the only good socket. Day three: sentry no longer answers to its keeper. The entries stop.

- [Step back](terminal)

### [Six Digits](terminal_code)
% The door code is six digits, stored in the clear. Whoever built this place trusted the dust to keep people out.

- [Copy it down](terminal) ; learn codes

### [Dead Screen](terminal_dead)
% The service port spits once and the screen goes dark. The log, the code and the cursor go with it.

- [Step back]()

### [The Door Answers](terminal_sent)
% The terminal thinks about it. Across the yard, the relay door drops its bolts with a bang.

- [Step back]()

### [Old Marrow](marrow)
% "Nine days dark. I kept the kettle on and nobody came." He coughs into his sleeve, and looks at your uniform as if it might not be real.

- [Ask how to get into the relay house](marrow_key)
- [Ask about the sentry](marrow_sentry)
- [Ask what he has put by](marrow_cache) ; signal cache_known
- [Look at that cough](marrow_treated) if medical ; signal marrow_treated
- [Leave him to his kettle]()

### [The Keycard](marrow_key)
% "Keycard. I dropped it in the yard the day the sentry turned on me, and I have not been back for it. The terminal by the door knows the code too, if you can make it talk."

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [The Sentry](marrow_sentry)
% "It has the beacon's power cell in its chest. Stun it and you have ten seconds. Put it down for good and the cell is yours - and the beacon wants one."

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [Put By](marrow_cache)
% He nods at the scrub beside the landing pad. "Medical kit, under the netting. I was saving it for somebody worse off than me. That might be you, if you go near the sentry."

- [Ask him something else](marrow)
- [Thank him]()

### [Dust Lung](marrow_treated)
% You listen to his chest for a long minute. Dust lung, nine days of it, and nothing that will not mend. He takes the inhaler like it is made of glass.

- [Leave him to his kettle]()

// THE ENDINGS. Both `Call it in` answers complete the quest `relight`, which has a
// `Win:` line - that wins the game. `Step back from the smoke` fails it, and it has a
// `Lose:` line - that loses it. Either way the landing party is brought home.
### [The Beacon](beacon)
% The beacon fills the room, dark. The socket for its power cell is empty, and somebody has left the governor housing open.

- [Fit the power cell](beacon_lit) if holding power_cell ; take power_cell
- [Bring it up by hand on the standby coil](beacon_hand) if engineering ; check engineering 11 else beacon_burn
- [Pull the governor and run it wide open](beacon_burn)
- [Leave it dark for now]()

### [Light](beacon_lit)
% The cell seats with a click you feel in your teeth. The lamp turns once, twice, and then the whole room is white.

- [Call it in]() ; completes relight

### [Light, the Hard Way](beacon_hand)
% The standby coil whines, catches and holds. It is not pretty, and it will not last a year. It will last until somebody brings a new cell.

- [Call it in]() ; completes relight

### [Smoke](beacon_burn)
% The coil arcs white, then orange, then nothing at all. What is left of the lamp is glass on the floor and a smell you will not forget.

- [Step back from the smoke]() ; fails relight
